          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "code": {
          "text": "Chest tightness, assessed as likely anxiety-related"
        },
        "verificationStatus": {
          "coding": [
            {
              "system": "http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/condition-ver-status",
              "code": "provisional"
            }
          ]
        },
        "note": [
          {
            "text": "Brief, non-exertional, unchanged pattern with previously normal cardiac workup. Low suspicion of ACS today; ACS/angina and arrhythmia considered less likely, PE unlikely. Age and risk factors warrant ongoing vigilance."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-1",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-1",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported anxiety symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "More on edge over the last few weeks; excessive worry most days, worse in the evenings and overnight. Worries about everything, particularly memory, heart disease and cancer, and fears medicines might be masking something serious."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-2",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-2",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Sleep symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Takes longer to fall asleep; wakes 1–2 times per night with worry and settles after staff reassurance. No nightmares."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-3",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-3",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Chest tightness and fluttering"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Intermittent mild chest tightness and fluttering when anxious, lasting minutes and settling with slow breathing and staff presence. Similar pattern for years, without clear exertional component, radiation, diaphoresis, nausea, vomiting or collapse."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-4",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-4",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported mood and enjoyment"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mood a bit low some days; still enjoys chats and television. No anhedonia across all activities."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-5",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-5",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Suicidal ideation and recorded attempt history"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies suicidal ideation today, saying 'I wouldnt do that to the kids'. No past attempts recorded."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-6",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-6",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported cognitive symptoms and trajectory"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Aware of cognitive decline and reports losing words more often, with worry about rapid deterioration. Mild forgetfulness noted. Staff report no acute stepwise cognitive change."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Functional support needs"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Needs assistance with instrumental activities of daily living and supervision of medicines and finances; orientation to date is variable."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Health-anxious behaviours"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Repeated requests over the past week for staff to check blood pressure and pulse in case of a heart attack. Googling health information on daughter's iPad and repeatedly questioning whether chest symptoms represent cancer or a heart attack. Some tangential concerns about water smelling funny and an extra evening cup of tea affecting nerves or heart."
      }
    },
    {
